{
  "comment": "Breakline curated RMM catalog. Domains sourced 'lolrmm:<slug>' come from lolrmm_snapshot.json (LOLRMM, Apache-2.0, see NOTICE); URL sources are vendor documentation. Ports are the tool's service ports. A port with scope 'tool_ips' is shared with ordinary traffic (80, 443, 8443 and so on) and only matters towards the tool's own resolved IPs and CIDRs. A port with scope 'any' is used only by RMM tools, so the gateway drops it towards any destination while locked, which also stops direct peer-to-peer sessions. Each domain has a 'channel': 'control' for remote-control traffic, 'management' for agent check-in, patching and monitoring, or 'both' where the sources do not say which (the default when missing). It is recorded only, never used to block, so pilot data can show whether the two can be told apart (D51, D52); 'channel_source' names the doc used to decide when it differs from 'source'.",
